  "text_md": "# RASIRC® BRUTE® Hydrazine <u>Hydrazine Gas Delivery</u>\n\n**Table 3: Specifications**\n\n|Operating Conditions|• Temperature: 10-40°C (Heaters must have secondary interlock) • Max Pressure: 1500 torr • Pneumatic Valve Actuation Pressure: 70 to 110 psig|\n|---|---|\n|Carrier Gas|• 0-500 sccm (user supplied MFC) • Filtered to 0.003 µm • Purified to < 1ppb contaminates • Nitrogen or inert gas (NO OXYGEN)|\n|Vapor Pressure|• 31 torr at 40°C • 13 torr at 25°C See Figure 1 for graph|\n|Tools & Supplies Required|• PPE (see SDS) • (2) 1/4” SS VCR gaskets no silver plating (Swagelok PN:SS-4-VCR-2-VS) • 3/4” and 5/8” wrenches|\n|Required Facilities|• Facility approved abatement system for hydrazine • Hydrazine safety gas monitor • Electrical ground connection • Proper ventilation|\n\n## How to Order\n\nTo place an order for **BRUTE Hydrazine** refer to Table 3 below. Choose the mass of solution desired and contact RASIRC at sales@rasirc.com to order the associated part numbers.\n\n**Table 4: BRUTE Hydrazine Vessel Rental**\n\n|Name|Mass of Solution|Chemistry Part Number|Lid Type|Vessel Part Number|\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n|BRUTE Hydrazine Vessel|250g 1000g|100723 100825|Standard Standard|100834 100857|\n\n## About RASIRC\n\nRASIRC specializes in products that generate and deliver gas to fabrication processes. Each unit is a dynamic gas plant in a box— converting common liquid chemistries into safe and reliable gas flow for most processes. RASIRC technology delivers water vapor, hydrogen peroxide gas and hydrazine gas in controlled, repeatable concentrations. RASIRC gas delivery systems, humidifiers, and closed loop humidification systems are critical for many applications in semiconductor, photovoltaic, pharmaceutical, medical, biological, fuel cell, and power industries.\n",
